  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "When parallel parking on a road with a continuous dividing line, a driver must position their vehicle at least 3 meters from the dividing line. This requirement is specified in the ACT Road Rules (Doc 2) to ensure there is enough space for other vehicles to pass safely.",
  "general_tip": "",
  "evidence": [
    "(6) If the road has a continuous dividing line or a dividing strip, the driver must position the vehicle at least 3m from the continuous dividing line or dividing strip, unless otherwise indicated by information on or with a parking control sign.",
    "(12) In this section:"
  ],
